<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel Bank buys IBM system for S$12 mln.</title>
<headline>Keppel Bank buys IBM system for S$12 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Keppel Bank said on Wednesday it signed a Singapore $12 million contract with International Business Machines Corp (IBM) for a computer system providing sales and servicing support for its staff at branches.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement the customised branch system would enable its staff to provide customers with comprehensive product information, financial analysis and planning, loans and deposits balance information and historical records at the touch of a button.</p>
<p>The entire system would be in place by the end of 1998.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
